  "description": "Per phase trading with mixed vehicles: cp01 is a single phase vehicle on L1 (own per phase limit 32A) and cp02 a three phase vehicle (16A). The grid node allows 32A per phase. cp02 takes its full 16A on all phases; cp01 receives the remaining 16A of L1 capacity, so L1 sums exactly to the grid limit. Under the legacy symmetric model cp01's draw would have been booked on all three phases and the pair could not both charge at these currents.",
